<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Disabled is asserted; Outputs OFF; Valve Status shown but Alarms disabled]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OFF-SCAN (EnableIn is False) STATUS
============================================================
Handle "NO MODE" Selection using the standard P_Mode AOI (EnableInFalse Routine, false scan required!).

NOTE:  IN ORDER TO AVOID USING AN "AFI" (which will generate a routine verify warning),
THIS RUNG USES AN XIC of Cfg_PCmdClear, followed by an XIO of the SAME BIT
to ensure P_Mode is SCANNED FALSE ("NO MODE").

THIS IS NOT DEAD CODE AND MUST APPEAR EXACTLY AS SHOWN FOR PROPER OPERATION!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration still needs to happen, even when device is disabled.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCmd_Stop  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTU(PCmd_Open)OTU(PCmd_Close)OTU(PCmd_Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_Open) OTU(OCmd_Close) OTU(OCmd_Stop) ,OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) OTU(MCmd_Disable) OTU(MCmd_Enable) ,OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Override Command is set to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[ 
Since we're not processing Operator Commands, we're not READY for them either!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Rdy_Open) OTU(Rdy_Close) OTU(Rdy_Stop) ,OTU(Rdy_Bypass) OTU(Rdy_Check) OTU(Rdy_Disable) OTU(Rdy_Enable) ,OTU(Rdy_Reset) OTU(Rdy_ResetAckAll) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
LIMIT SWITCH FEEDBACK DETERMINATION
============================================================
This first "Open" feedback is a copy of the Open Limit Switch, if it is being
used, or a copy of the OPPOSITE of the Closed Limit Switch, if ONLY the
Closed Limit Switch is being used.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIC(Inp_OpenLS) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIC(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIO(Inp_ClosedLS) ]OTE(Wrk_OpenFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This first "Closed" feedback is a copy of the Closed Limit Switch, if it is being
used, or a copy of the OPPOSITE of the Open Limit Switch, if ONLY the
Open Limit Switch is being used.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIC(Inp_ClosedLS) ,XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIC(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIO(Inp_OpenLS) ]OTE(Wrk_ClosedFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE FEEDBACK STATUS
============================================================
This rung generates the Valve Feedback Status bits and Enumeration Value:
Limit Switch Fail, if the Limit Switches are in the fail position (won't be seen in Simulation)
Opened, if the valve is confirmed opened
Closed, if the valve is confirmed closed
Moving, if the Limit Switches show travel]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) [[XIC(Cfg_LSFail) XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_LSFail) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ] OTE(Sts_LSFail) MOV(3,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) OTE(Sts_Opened) MOV(2,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) OTE(Sts_Closed) MOV(1,Val_Fdbk) ] ,[[XIC(Cfg_LSFail) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_LSFail) XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ] ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] OTE(Sts_Stopped) CLR(Val_Fdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Reset the fault condition and simulation / command retrigger timers.

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[RES(Wrk_FullStallT) RES(Wrk_TransitStallT) RES(Wrk_SimOpenT) RES(Wrk_SimCloseT) ,RES(Wrk_OpenPulseT) RES(Wrk_ClosePulseT) RES(Wrk_StopPulseT) ,OTU(Wrk_Open) OTU(Wrk_Close) OTL(Wrk_Stop) ,OTU(Wrk_OpenOut) OTU(Wrk_CloseOut) OTU(Wrk_StopOut) ,OTU(Wrk_SimOpenOut) OTU(Wrk_SimOpenLS) OTU(Wrk_SimCloseOut) OTU(Wrk_SimClosedLS) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Outputs are cleared when Disabled (EnableInFalse).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out_Open)OTU(Out_Close)OTU(Out_Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the motor as Disabled and Not Ready, not Available, and with no
Maintenance Bypass breadcrumb.
Clear remaining Status bits.
Show the enumerated valve command as NONE.
Show the enumerated valve status as DISABLED.
Show the enumerated valve fault status as NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(Sts_Disabled) OTL(Sts_NotRdy) OTU(Sts_Available) OTU(Sts_MaintByp) ,OTL(Nrdy_NoMode) OTU(Nrdy_Disabled) OTU(Nrdy_CfgErr) OTU(Nrdy_Perm) ,OTU(Nrdy_EqpFault) OTU(Nrdy_Fail) OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ,OTU(Sts_CmdToOpen) OTU(Sts_Opening) OTU(Sts_CmdToClose) OTU(Sts_Closing) ,CLR(Val_Cmd) MOV(33,Val_Sts) CLR(Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the Alarms and the Notify Status, and show the Alarms Inhibited breadcrumb.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Alm_FullStall) OTU(Alm_TransitStall) OTU(Alm_ActuatorFault) OTU(Alm_IOFault) ,OTU(Sts_FullStall) OTU(Sts_TransitStall) OTU(Sts_ActuatorFault) OTU(Sts_IOFault) ,OTL(Sts_AlmInh) CLR(Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED STATUS VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_InpPV
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_SrcQ) ,[XIO(Cfg_HasOpenLS) ,XIO(Cfg_HasClosedLS) ] MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIO(Cfg_HasOpenLS) XIO(Cfg_HasClosedLS) MOV(2,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(9,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(20,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Normal Scan: control / monitor solenoid-operated valve]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_ValveMO:  PROCESS -- MOTOR OPERATED VALVE
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V1.x, V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib. Using P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.0.
Added PCmd_Stop.
V3.0-01  2013-07-31:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-02  2013-09-03:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-03  2013-10-30:  Corrected Parameter descriptions and
default configuration values for alarms only.
V3.0-04  2014-01-22:  Modified to ensure PCmd_Stop beats
PCmd_Open / PCmd_Close
V3.1-00  2014-07-08:  Modified to use P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1; added
Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_Xxxxx), source/quality values
(SrcQ). Modified to consistently use alias tag names.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Exposed stall timers ACC/PRE (read-only). Corrections to
Nrdy_  trip and reset logic. Using P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1-01.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
This Instruction controls and monitors a motor-operated
valve (typ. two position: opened, closed) and provides:

*  Ability to command valve to open, command valve to close, and,
optionally, command valve to stop motion
*  Ability to reverse valve travel (for valves with the ability to accept a Stop output)
*  Monitoring of limit switch feedback, display of actual valve status
*  Detection of failure to move (full stall), failure to reach position (transit stall)
*  Monitoring of Permissive conditions to motor the valve open, and separate
Permissive conditions to motor the valve closed
*  Simulation, providing feedback of a working valve while disabling outputs
*  Monitoring of I/O communication faults
*  Alarms for Full Stall, Transit Stall, Actuator Failure (separate input), I/O Fault
*  "Available" status for use by automation logic to know whether valve
      can be controlled by other objects.

Modes are provided by a P_Mode AOI instance.
Alarms are provided by P_Alarm AOI instances.
Modes of operation: Operator, Program, Override, Maintenance, Hand
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MODE PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung handles received Mode Inputs and Commands:

NOTE:  All Commands for Mode, Alarm are aliased directly to the
corresponding Commands in the contained P_Mode and P_Alarm AOIs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles simple First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION PROCESSING
============================================================
If the Valve does not have an Open Limit Switch input,
it cannot be used for Valve feedback checking.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Cfg_HasOpenLS)OTU(Cfg_UseOpenLS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Valve does not have a Closed Limit Switch input,
it cannot be used for Valve feedback checking.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Cfg_HasClosedLS)OTU(Cfg_UseClosedLS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Enter the time (in seconds) for the Valve to successfully move from its starting position before declaring a fault.
Enter the time (in seconds) for the Valve to successfully reach its target position before declaring a fault.
Enter the time (in seconds) to pulse the valve outputs (Out_Open, Out_Close and Out_Stop)
(zero - held on continuously)

If the timer preset calcuated wraps negative (more than 2.14... million seconds), then max out the
Timer Preset.  Note that a negative timer preset will fault the controller!!!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[MUL(Cfg_FullStallT,1000,Wrk_FullStallT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_FullStallT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_FullStallT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_TransitStallT,1000,Wrk_TransitStallT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_TransitStallT.PRE.31) MOV(2147483647,Wrk_TransitStallT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_OutPulseT,1000,Wrk_OpenPulseT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_OpenPulseT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_OpenPulseT.PRE) ] OTE(Err_Timer) ,MOV(Wrk_OpenPulseT.PRE,Wrk_ClosePulseT.PRE) MOV(Wrk_OpenPulseT.PRE,Wrk_StopPulseT.PRE) ,EQU(Wrk_StopPulseT.PRE,0) MOV(5000,Wrk_StopPulseT.PRE) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Enter the time (in seconds) to echo back the desired state when Opened or Closed in simulation

Handle timer preset invalid values as above.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MUL(Cfg_SimFdbkT,1000,Wrk_SimOpenT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_SimOpenT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_SimOpenT.PRE) OTE(Err_Sim) ,MOV(Wrk_SimOpenT.PRE,Wrk_SimCloseT.PRE) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung generates a summary Bad Config status, simply an OR of the individual bits provided above
(in the Configuration handling section).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Err_Timer) ,XIC(Err_Sim) ,[XIC(FullStall.Sts_Err) ,XIC(TransitStall.Sts_Err) ,XIC(ActuatorFault.Sts_Err) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_Err) ] OTE(Err_Alarm) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SIMULATION TIMERS
============================================================
If the (simulated) Open output was sent to the valve, run the Open Simulation Timer.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_SimOpenOut)XIO(Wrk_StopOut)TON(Wrk_SimOpenT,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the (simulated) Open output was sent to the valve, run the Open Simulation Timer.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_SimCloseOut)XIO(Wrk_StopOut)TON(Wrk_SimCloseT,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When 1/4 of the valve simulation open time has expired, move off the simulated closed limit switch.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CMP(Wrk_SimOpenT.ACC>(Wrk_SimOpenT.PRE/4))[XIC(Cfg_LSFail) OTU(Wrk_SimClosedLS) ,XIO(Cfg_LSFail) OTL(Wrk_SimOpenLS) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When 1/4 of the valve simulation close time has expired, move off the simulated open limit switch.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CMP(Wrk_SimCloseT.ACC>(Wrk_SimCloseT.PRE/4))[XIC(Cfg_LSFail) OTU(Wrk_SimOpenLS) ,XIO(Cfg_LSFail) OTL(Wrk_SimClosedLS) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When the valve simulation open time has expired, move onto the simulated open limit switch.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_SimOpenT.DN)OTU(Wrk_SimOpenOut)OTL(Wrk_SimOpenLS)OTU(Wrk_SimClosedLS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[When the valve simulation close time has expired, move onto the simulated closed limit switch.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_SimCloseT.DN)OTU(Wrk_SimCloseOut)OTL(Wrk_SimClosedLS)OTU(Wrk_SimOpenLS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE FEEDBACK PROCESSING
============================================================
If the Valve is NOT being simulated and it HAS and IS USING limit switch feedback,
use the state of the limit switch feedback inputs as the Valve position.

If the Valve is being simulated or has no limit switch feedback, use the Sim Timers to provide
"fake" feedback signals based on the simulation time to Open and time to Close.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIC(Inp_OpenLS) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIC(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIO(Inp_ClosedLS) ] ,[XIC(Inp_Sim) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) ] XIC(Wrk_SimOpenLS) ]OTE(Wrk_OpenFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Valve is NOT being simulated and it HAS and IS USING limit switch feedback,
use the state of the limit switch feedback inputs as the Valve position.

If the Valve is being simulated or has no limit switch feedback, use the Sim Timers to provide
"fake" feedback signals based on the simulation time to Open and time to Close.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Inp_Sim) [XIC(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIC(Inp_ClosedLS) ,XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIC(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIO(Inp_OpenLS) ] ,[XIC(Inp_Sim) ,XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) ] XIC(Wrk_SimClosedLS) ]OTE(Wrk_ClosedFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung generates the Valve Feedback Status bits and Enumeration Value:
Limit Switch Fail, if the Limit Switches are in the fail position (won't be seen in Simulation)
Opened, if the valve is confirmed opened
Closed, if the valve is confirmed closed
Moving, if the Limit Switches show travel]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Cfg_LSFail) XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_LSFail) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ] OTE(Sts_LSFail) MOV(3,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) MOV(2,Val_Fdbk) ,XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) MOV(1,Val_Fdbk) ,[XIC(Cfg_LSFail) XIO(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIO(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ,XIO(Cfg_LSFail) XIC(Wrk_OpenFdbk) XIC(Wrk_ClosedFdbk) ] CLR(Val_Fdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
INTERLOCK / PERMISSIVE BYPASS / CHECK COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Bypass Command bypasses the Bypassable Permissives and Interlocks.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Bypass)OTU(OCmd_Bypass)OTL(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Check Command enables checking of ALL
Permissives and Interlocks (cancels the bypass).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(OCmd_Check)OTU(OCmd_Check)OTU(Wrk_Bypass);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Bypass flag is set, Bypassable Interlocks and Permissives ARE BYPASSED.
Bypassing is ACTIVE if Bypass selected OR in Maintenance Mode,
or in Override Mode if Override Bypassing is configured.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Sts_Bypass) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ,XIC(Sts_Ovrd) XIC(Cfg_OvrdPerm) ]OTE(Sts_BypActive);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Maintenance Bypass function is active, display the Maintenance Bypass
Indicator (triangle symbol) on the graphic symbol.  Bypass functions are:
*  Interlock / Permissive Bypass function is enabled
*  Valve HAS opened position feedback designated by engineer, but
maintenance has selected to NOT USE opened position feedback
*  Valve HAS closed position feedback designated by engineer, but
maintenance has selected to NOT USE closed position feedback]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Bypass) ,XIC(Cfg_HasOpenLS) XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) ,XIC(Cfg_HasClosedLS) XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) ]OTE(Sts_MaintByp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready for Interlock / Permissive Bypass if not bypassed.
Ready to cancel Bypass (resume checking) if bypassed.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Bypass) ,XIC(Wrk_Bypass) OTE(Rdy_Check) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE DISABLE/ENABLE COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Disable Command disables the Analog Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Disable)OTU(MCmd_Disable)XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)OTL(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Enable Command cancels the Disable and enables the Analog Output.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCmd_Enable)OTU(MCmd_Enable)XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)OTU(Wrk_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the internal Disabled flag is set, the motor is DISABLED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Disabled)OTE(Sts_Disabled);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready to Disable device if in Maintenance Mode and device is NOT Disabled.
Ready to Enable device if in Maintenance Mode and device IS Disabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Mode.Rdy_MRel)[XIO(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Disable) ,XIC(Wrk_Disabled) OTE(Rdy_Enable) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM RESET COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
This rung handles the Alarm Reset Input and Commands
and the "Reset and Ack All" Operator Command.

This rung processes received Reset Commands from:

1.  The Operator via HMI Operator Command, or
2.  Higher-level strategies via Program Command
3.  Pushbuttons or other block via Input
4.  Resets initiated by other device Operator Commands (if configured to do so)
and forwards the Reset to ALL Alarms and latched Shed conditions.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,[XIC(OCmd_Open) ,XIC(OCmd_Close) ,XIC(OCmd_Stop) ] XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) [OTL(PCmd_FullStallAck) ,OTL(PCmd_TransitStallAck) ,OTL(PCmd_ActuatorFaultAck) ,OTL(PCmd_IOFaultAck) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Reset) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ][OTL(FullStall.PCmd_Reset) OTL(TransitStall.PCmd_Reset) OTL(ActuatorFault.PCmd_Reset) OTL(IOFault.PCmd_Reset) ,XIC(Sts_FullStall) RES(Wrk_FullStallT) ,XIC(Sts_TransitStall) RES(Wrk_TransitStallT) ,OTU(Nrdy_Fail) ,[XIO(Inp_ActuatorFault) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] OTU(Nrdy_EqpFault) ,[XIO(Inp_IOFault) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE FULL STALL DETECTION
============================================================
If the Valve was told to Open and it hasn't moved off the Fully Closed position,
or if it was told to Close and it hasn't moved off the Fully Open position,
run the Full Stall Timer.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Open) EQU(Val_Fdbk,1) ,XIC(Wrk_Close) EQU(Val_Fdbk,2) ]XIO(Sts_Maint)XIO(Wrk_TransitStallT.DN)TON(Wrk_FullStallT,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Full Stall timer times out, the valve never moved when it was commanded.
If we're not in Maintenance mode, issue a Full Stall Status.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_FullStallT.DN)OTE(Sts_FullStall)XIC(Cfg_ShedOnFullStall)OTL(Nrdy_Fail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE TRANSIT STALL DETECTION
============================================================
If the Valve was told to Open and it hasn't reached fully Open,
or if it was told to Close and it hasn't reached fully Closed,
run the Transit Stall Timer.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_Open) NEQ(Val_Fdbk,2) ,XIC(Wrk_Close) NEQ(Val_Fdbk,1) ]XIO(Sts_Maint)XIO(Wrk_FullStallT.DN)TON(Wrk_TransitStallT,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Transit Stall timer times out and we're not in Maintenance Mode,
raise the Transit Stall Status (valve moved but did not reach target).

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_TransitStallT.DN)OTE(Sts_TransitStall)XIC(Cfg_ShedOnTransitStall)OTL(Nrdy_Fail);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Valve is NOT READY if Interlocks are not OK, Permissives do not allow
the valve to move, there is a latched Fault, the valve is disabled, or
there is a configuration error.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_NoMode)[XIC(Sts_Disabled) OTE(Nrdy_Disabled) ,XIC(Sts_Err) OTE(Nrdy_CfgErr) ,[[XIO(Inp_ClosePermOK) XIO(Sts_BypActive) ,XIO(Inp_CloseNBPermOK) ] XIO(Sts_CmdToClose) XIO(Sts_Closing) XIO(Sts_Closed) ,[XIO(Inp_OpenPermOK) XIO(Sts_BypActive) ,XIO(Inp_OpenNBPermOK) ] XIO(Sts_CmdToOpen) XIO(Sts_Opening) XIO(Sts_Opened) ] OTE(Nrdy_Perm) ,XIC(Inp_ActuatorFault) XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Sts_ActuatorFault) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnActuatorFault) OTL(Nrdy_EqpFault) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Sts_IOFault) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnIOFault) OTL(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTE(Wrk_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALVE COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
The Valve is NOT READY if Interlocks are not OK, Permissives do not allow
the valve to move, there is a latched Fault, the valve is disabled, or
there is a configuration error.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_NotRdy) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_EqpFault) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) ]OTE(Sts_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The device is AVAILABLE to be controlled by other objects
if it IS in Program Mode and it IS NOT "Not Ready".]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Prog)XIO(Sts_NotRdy)OTE(Sts_Available);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These next rungs, in priority order, determine whether the valve should be open or closed.

If a Valve OPEN command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override State is OPEN, mark the valve TO OPEN.
(Modes are mutually exclusive, thus handling the priority.)

#####  V3.0-04  2014-01-20:  Modified to ensure PCmd_Stop beats PCmd_Open / PCmd_Close  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Open) OTU(OCmd_Open) XIO(OCmd_Stop) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) RES(Wrk_OpenPulseT) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Open) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Open) ,NOP() ] XIO(PCmd_Stop) XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,2) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ][XIC(Inp_OpenPermOK) ,XIC(Sts_BypActive) ]XIC(Inp_OpenNBPermOK)[[XIO(Sts_CmdToOpen) XIO(Sts_Opening) [XIO(Sts_CmdToClose) XIO(Sts_Closing) ,XIC(Cfg_HasStop) ] ,XIC(Sts_TransitStall) ,XIC(Sts_FullStall) ] XIO(Sts_Opened) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ][OTU(Wrk_StopOut) ,[XIC(Sts_CmdToClose) ,XIC(Sts_Closing) ] OTL(Wrk_StopOut) ][OTU(Wrk_Close) OTU(Wrk_CloseOut) OTU(Wrk_SimCloseOut) ,OTL(Wrk_Open) OTL(Wrk_OpenOut) OTL(Wrk_SimOpenOut) ,OTU(Wrk_Stop) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Valve CLOSE command is received in Operator, Program or Maintenance
Mode, or if in Override Mode and the Override State is CLOSE, mark the valve TO CLOSE.
(Modes are mutually exclusive, thus handling the priority.)

#####  V3.0-04  2014-01-20:  Modified to ensure PCmd_Stop beats PCmd_Open / PCmd_Close  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Close) OTU(OCmd_Close) XIO(OCmd_Stop) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) RES(Wrk_ClosePulseT) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Close) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Close) ,NOP() ] XIO(PCmd_Stop) XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,1) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ][XIC(Inp_ClosePermOK) ,XIC(Sts_BypActive) ]XIC(Inp_CloseNBPermOK)[[[XIO(Sts_CmdToOpen) XIO(Sts_Opening) ,XIC(Cfg_HasStop) ] XIO(Sts_CmdToClose) XIO(Sts_Closing) ,XIC(Sts_TransitStall) ,XIC(Sts_FullStall) ] XIO(Sts_Closed) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ][OTU(Wrk_StopOut) ,[XIC(Sts_CmdToOpen) ,XIC(Sts_Opening) ] OTL(Wrk_StopOut) ][OTL(Wrk_Close) OTL(Wrk_CloseOut) OTL(Wrk_SimCloseOut) ,OTU(Wrk_Open) OTU(Wrk_OpenOut) OTU(Wrk_SimOpenOut) ,OTU(Wrk_Stop) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Stop command is received in Operator, Maintenance or Override Mode,
flag the Valve to STOP.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCmd_Stop  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Stop) OTU(OCmd_Stop) [XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) RES(Wrk_StopPulseT) ] ,[XIC(PCmd_Stop) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Stop) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(PCmd_Open) XIC(PCmd_Close) XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear) ] XIC(Sts_Prog) ,EQU(Inp_OvrdCmd,3) CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd) XIC(Sts_Ovrd) ][XIO(Sts_Opened) XIO(Sts_Closed) XIO(Sts_Stopped) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) XIO(Wrk_StopOut) ][OTU(Wrk_Close) OTU(Wrk_CloseOut) OTU(Wrk_SimCloseOut) ,OTU(Wrk_Open) OTU(Wrk_OpenOut) OTU(Wrk_SimOpenOut) ,OTL(Wrk_Stop) OTL(Wrk_StopOut) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Higher Priority: HAND always wins over other Modes:
If in Hand, have the Valve follow the position feedback.
If the valve is confirmed Opened, set to Open.
If the valve is confirmed Closed, set to Close
If the valve has no feedback, or if no position is confirmed, set to STOPPED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Hand) ,XIC(S:FS) ][EQU(Val_Fdbk,2) OTL(Wrk_Open) OTL(Wrk_SimOpenLS) OTU(Wrk_Close) OTU(Wrk_SimClosedLS) OTU(Wrk_Stop) ,EQU(Val_Fdbk,1) OTU(Wrk_Open) OTU(Wrk_SimOpenLS) OTL(Wrk_Close) OTL(Wrk_SimClosedLS) OTU(Wrk_Stop) ,[EQU(Val_Fdbk,0) ,EQU(Val_Fdbk,3) ,XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) ] OTU(Wrk_Open) OTU(Wrk_SimOpenLS) OTU(Wrk_Close) OTU(Wrk_SimClosedLS) OTL(Wrk_Stop) ,OTU(Wrk_OpenOut) OTU(Wrk_SimOpenOut) OTU(Wrk_CloseOut) OTU(Wrk_SimCloseOut) OTU(Wrk_StopOut) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Highest Priority:
If the Valve has a Shed Fault OR if the Valve is Disabled or
has a Configuration Error, stop the valve.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_NotRdy)[OTU(Wrk_Open) OTU(Wrk_OpenOut) OTU(Wrk_SimOpenOut) ,OTU(Wrk_Close) OTU(Wrk_CloseOut) OTU(Wrk_SimCloseOut) ,OTL(Wrk_Stop) OTL(Wrk_StopOut) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OUTPUT GENERATION
============================================================
If the Valve should be Opened and not Stopped (for change of direction),
run the OPEN Pulse Timer

If the Valve should be Closed and not Stopped (for change of direction),
run the CLOSE Pulse Timer

If the Valve should be Stopped, run the STOP Pulse Timer.
When the timer is DONE, if we ARE doing a Change of Direction,
continue by Opening or Closing the valve (as appropriate) and turn off the STOP request.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_OpenOut) XIO(Wrk_StopOut) [TON(Wrk_OpenPulseT,?,?) ,GRT(Wrk_OpenPulseT.PRE,0) [XIO(Sts_Maint) EQU(Val_Fdbk,2) ,XIC(Wrk_OpenPulseT.DN) ] OTU(Wrk_OpenOut) ] ,XIC(Wrk_CloseOut) XIO(Wrk_StopOut) [TON(Wrk_ClosePulseT,?,?) ,GRT(Wrk_ClosePulseT.PRE,0) [XIO(Sts_Maint) EQU(Val_Fdbk,1) ,XIC(Wrk_ClosePulseT.DN) ] OTU(Wrk_CloseOut) ] ,XIC(Wrk_StopOut) [TON(Wrk_StopPulseT,?,?) ,[XIO(Cfg_HasStop) ,XIC(Wrk_StopPulseT.DN) ] OTU(Wrk_StopOut) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Valve is NOT SIMULATED, NOT FAULTED and NOT DISABLED, generate the
appropriate outputs for the Valve.

If the Valve should be Opened and not Stopped, energize the
Out_Open Output until we get feedback that the Valve is Opened
or the pulse time is done.

If the Valve should be Closed and not Stopped, energize the
Out_Close Output until we get feedback that the Valve is Closed
or the pulse time is done.

If the Valve should be Stopped, energize Out_Stop for the full pulse duration.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)XIO(Nrdy_Fail)XIO(Nrdy_EqpFault)XIO(Nrdy_IOFault)XIO(Sts_Disabled)XIO(Sts_Err)[XIC(Wrk_OpenOut) XIO(Wrk_StopOut) OTE(Out_Open) ,XIC(Wrk_CloseOut) XIO(Wrk_StopOut) OTE(Out_Close) ,XIC(Wrk_StopOut) XIC(Cfg_HasStop) OTE(Out_Stop) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
DEVICE STATUS GENERATION
============================================================
Val_Cmd is the currently-executing command:
0 = None
1 = Close
2 = Open
3 = Stop

Val_Sts is the current device status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = Powerup / Unknown
1 = Closed
2 = Opened
3 = Commanded to Close
4 = Commanded to Open
5 = Closing
6 = Opening
7 = Stopped
33 = Device Disabled

Val_Fault is the current device fault status, as determined by this AOI,
based on its knowledge of commands executed and feedback.
(This is the fault status that should be monitored by, for example, FT Historian.)
0 = None
16 = Full Stall
17 = Transit Stall
32 = I/O Fault (from Input)
34 = Configuration Error]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Wrk_Cmd)CLR(Wrk_Sts)CLR(Wrk_Fault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These rungs generate the Stopped, Commanded to Openm Opening, Opened,
Commanded to Close, Closing and Closed Status bits.

If the Valve is in HAND and HAS NO POSITION FEEDBACK, its state is meaningless;
turn off ALL the Sts_xxx states!!!!!

If the valve is told to stop, show the valve as STOPPED, unless the feedbacks
confirm it is fully opened or fully closed -- then show it as such.

If the Valve is commanded to Open and the feedback shows it hasn't moved yet,
the Valve is COMMANDED TO OPEN.

If the Valve is commanded to Open and the feedback doesn't yet show it Opened,
the Valve is OPENING.

If the Valve is commanded to Open and the feedback shows it Opened,
the Valve is OPENED.

If the Valve is commanded to Close and the feedback shows it hasn't moved yet,
the Valve is COMMANDED TO CLOSE.

If the Valve is commanded to Close and the feedback does not show Closed,
the Valve is CLOSING.

If the Valve is commanded to Close and the feedback shows it has Closed,
the Valve is CLOSED.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Sts_Hand) ,XIC(Cfg_UseOpenLS) ,XIC(Cfg_UseClosedLS) ][XIC(Wrk_Stop) OTE(Sts_Stopped) MOV(7,Wrk_Sts) [EQU(Val_Fdbk,2) OTL(Wrk_Open) OTU(Wrk_Close) ,EQU(Val_Fdbk,1) OTL(Wrk_Close) OTU(Wrk_Open) ] OTU(Wrk_Stop) ,XIO(Wrk_Stop) [XIC(Wrk_Open) [EQU(Val_Fdbk,1) OTE(Sts_CmdToOpen) MOV(4,Wrk_Sts) ,EQU(Val_Fdbk,0) OTE(Sts_Opening) MOV(6,Wrk_Sts) ,EQU(Val_Fdbk,2) OTE(Sts_Opened) MOV(2,Wrk_Sts) ] ,XIC(Wrk_Close) [EQU(Val_Fdbk,2) OTE(Sts_CmdToClose) MOV(3,Wrk_Sts) ,EQU(Val_Fdbk,0) OTE(Sts_Closing) MOV(5,Wrk_Sts) ,EQU(Val_Fdbk,1) OTE(Sts_Closed) MOV(1,Wrk_Sts) ] ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles the remaining Val_Cmd, Val_Sts and Val_Fault enumerated values.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Sts_CmdToClose) ,XIC(Sts_Closing) ] MOV(1,Wrk_Cmd) ,[XIC(Sts_CmdToOpen) ,XIC(Sts_Opening) ] MOV(2,Wrk_Cmd) ,XIC(Wrk_StopOut) MOV(3,Wrk_Cmd) ,XIC(Sts_TransitStall) MOV(16,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_FullStall) MOV(17,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Nrdy_EqpFault) MOV(19,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) MOV(32,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_Disabled) MOV(33,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Err) MOV(34,Wrk_Fault) ,MOV(Wrk_Cmd,Val_Cmd) MOV(Wrk_Sts,Val_Sts) MOV(Wrk_Fault,Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED SOURCE / QUALITY VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality for Input / Output values / status (SrcQ_IO)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_SrcQ) ,[XIO(Cfg_HasOpenLS) ,XIO(Cfg_HasClosedLS) ] MOV(1,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIO(Cfg_HasOpenLS) XIO(Cfg_HasClosedLS) MOV(2,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_IOFault) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(9,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality for primary values / status (SrcQ)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(SrcQ_IO,Wrk_SrcQ) ,[XIC(Cfg_HasOpenLS) XIO(Cfg_UseOpenLS) ,XIC(Cfg_HasClosedLS) XIO(Cfg_UseClosedLS) ] MOV(18,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="46" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OPERATOR COMMAND READIES
============================================================
Ready to Open if in Operator Manual, Closed, and Permissives and Interlocks are OK.

Ready to Close if in Operator Manual and (Opened or Opening).

#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ trip and reset logic.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Oper) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ]XIO(Wrk_NotRdy)[XIO(Sts_NotRdy) ,XIC(Cfg_OCmdResets) ][[[XIO(Sts_CmdToOpen) XIO(Sts_Opening) [XIO(Sts_CmdToClose) XIO(Sts_Closing) ,XIC(Cfg_HasStop) ] ,XIC(Sts_TransitStall) ,XIC(Sts_FullStall) ] XIO(Sts_Opened) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] OTE(Rdy_Open) ,[[[XIO(Sts_CmdToOpen) XIO(Sts_Opening) ,XIC(Cfg_HasStop) ] XIO(Sts_CmdToClose) XIO(Sts_Closing) ,XIC(Sts_TransitStall) ,XIC(Sts_FullStall) ] XIO(Sts_Closed) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] OTE(Rdy_Close) ,XIC(Cfg_HasStop) [XIO(Sts_Opened) XIO(Sts_Closed) XIO(Sts_Stopped) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) XIO(Wrk_StopOut) ] OTE(Rdy_Stop) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="47" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM PROCESSING
============================================================
Pass the Cfg_PCmdClear configuration down to each P_Alarm instance.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(FullStall.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(TransitStall.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(ActuatorFault.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(IOFault.Cfg_PCmdClear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="48" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The various alarms are ALWAYS allowed to Exist (Cfg_HasXxxAlarm can be 1), EXCEPT:
* If the valve DOES NOT HAVE ANY POSITION FEEDBACK, the Full Stall alarm
will never occur and should not exist.
* If the valve DOES NOT HAVE BOTH POSITION FEEDBACKs, the Transit Stall alarm
will never occur and should not exist.
(If feedback exists, the stall alarms must be allowed to exist.)

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCfg_AllowExist on P_Alarm 3.0.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(ActuatorFault.PCfg_AllowExist) OTL(IOFault.PCfg_AllowExist) ,[XIC(Cfg_HasClosedLS) ,XIC(Cfg_HasOpenLS) ] OTE(FullStall.PCfg_AllowExist) ,XIC(Cfg_HasClosedLS) XIC(Cfg_HasOpenLS) OTE(TransitStall.PCfg_AllowExist) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="49" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM PROCESSING
============================================================
Handle Valve Full Stall (never moved) Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(FullStall);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="50" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Valve Transit Stall (moved but did not complete move)
Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(TransitStall);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="51" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Valve Actuator Fault Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(ActuatorFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="52" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle I/O Fault Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(IOFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="53" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If ANY alarm is Disabled, Inhibited or Suppressed, set the Alarm Inhibit
summary status bit (which puts the "I" box on the graphic symbol).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(TransitStall.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(FullStall.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(ActuatorFault.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(IOFault.Sts_AlmInh) ]OTE(Sts_AlmInh);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="54" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
NOTIFICATION VALUE
============================================================
Indicate the current alarm notification level as the max of any of the alarms,
and set the low-order bit for reset or ack required:
0 = Not in alarm, acknowledged
1 = Not in alarm, unacknowledged or reset required
2 = Low severity alarm, acknowledged
3 = Low severity alarm, unacknowledged
4 = Medium severity alarm, acknowledged
5 = Medium severity alarm, unacknowledged
6 = High severity alarm, acknowledged
7 = High severity alarm, unacknowledged
8 = Urgent severity alarm, acknowledged
9 = Urgent severity alarm, unacknowledged

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Separated Reset Reqd functions from Val_Notify  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(FullStall.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(FullStall.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(TransitStall.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(TransitStall.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(ActuatorFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(ActuatorFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(IOFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,[XIC(FullStall.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(TransitStall.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(ActuatorFault.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(IOFault.Val_Notify.0) ] OTE(Wrk_Notify.0) ,MOV(Wrk_Notify,Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="55" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung identifies:
* if any alarm reset or other reset is required; and
* if any reset or acknowledge from the operator is required.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx), split from Val_Notify logic (above).  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(FullStall.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(TransitStall.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(ActuatorFault.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Ack) ] ,[XIC(FullStall.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(TransitStall.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(ActuatorFault.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(IOFault.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(Nrdy_Fail) ,XIC(Nrdy_EqpFault) XIO(Sts_ActuatorFault) ,XIC(Nrdy_IOFault) XIO(Sts_IOFault) ] OTE(Rdy_Reset) ]OTE(Rdy_ResetAckAll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear Ownership, set to De-Energized state, clear "lurking" Commands]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PRESCAN (POWERUP) HANDLING
============================================================
On Prescan, set the Ownership to NO OWNER (0).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(PSet_Owner)CLR(Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCmd_Stop  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTU(PCmd_Open)OTU(PCmd_Close)OTU(PCmd_Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_Open) OTU(OCmd_Close) OTU(OCmd_Stop) OTU(OCmd_Bypass) OTU(OCmd_Check) ,OTU(MCmd_Disable) OTU(MCmd_Enable) OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Override Command is set to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Inp_OvrdCmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the latched valve commands and latched Shed faults,
and reset the simulated limit switches.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Wrk_Open) OTU(Wrk_Close) OTL(Wrk_Stop) ,OTU(Wrk_OpenOut) OTU(Wrk_CloseOut) OTU(Wrk_StopOut) ,OTU(Wrk_SimOpenOut) OTU(Wrk_SimOpenLS) OTU(Wrk_SimCloseOut) OTU(Wrk_SimClosedLS) ,OTU(Nrdy_Fail) OTU(Nrdy_EqpFault) OTU(Nrdy_IOFault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[All Outputs are de-energized on Prescan.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out_Open)OTU(Out_Close)OTU(Out_Stop);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[On Prescan, clear the following:
Val_Cmd (no command active)
Val_Fdbk (device position not determined)
Val_Sts (device status powerup / unknown)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Val_Cmd)CLR(Val_Fdbk)CLR(Val_Sts);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Alarm"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Mode"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
